<sect> angles (Revision 1.2 -- 06/05/98)
<p> This unit regroups some routines for dealing with different
representations of angles including the hexadecimal.

<sect1> Type Definitions
<p>

<sect2> struct hms

<p>The struct <tt/hms/, which stands for hour:minutes:seconds helds
the hexadecimal representation of an angle (<tt/deg/ = degrees, 
<tt/min/ = minutes, and <tt/sec/ = seconds).

<tscreen><verb>
struct hms {
    int deg;
    int min;
    double sec;
  } 
</verb></tscreen>

<sect2> struct Angle
<p> The struct Angle regroups all different representation of an
angle. <tt/rad/ = value in radian. <tt/grad/ = value in grad (one 
circle = 400 grad), <tt/deg/ =decimal value in degrees
(1 circle = 360 degrees), <tt/hms/ = hexademical representation
of the value with <tt/deg, min, sec/.

<tscreen><verb>
struct Angle {
  double rad;
  double grad;
  double deg;
  struct hms dms;
}
</verb></tscreen>


<sect1> Routines
<p>
<sect2> afromrad
<p>
<tscreen><verb>
struct Angle afromrad (double angrad)
</verb></tscreen>
<p>Fills all fields of the struct <tt/Angle/, given an angle <tt/angrad/ 
in radians.

<sect2> afromdeg
<p>
<tscreen><verb>
struct Angle afromdeg (double angdeg)
</verb></tscreen>
<p>Fills all fields of the struct <tt/Angle/, given an angle <tt/angdeg/ 
in degree (decimal value).


<sect2> afromgrad
<p>
<tscreen><verb>
struct Angle afromgrad(double anggrad)
</verb></tscreen>
<p>Fills all fields of the struct <tt/Angle/, given an angle <tt/anggrad/ 
in grad.


<sect2>afromdmsverb 
<p>
<tscreen><verb>
struct Angle afromdmsverb(int degrees, int minutes, double seconds)
</verb></tscreen>
<p>Fills all fields of the struct <tt/Angle/, given an angle
in hexadecimal representation (<tt/degrees, minutes/ <tt/seconds/).

<sect2>afromdms
<p>
<tscreen><verb>
struct Angle afromdms(struct hms mydms)
</verb></tscreen>
<p>Same as <tt/afromdmsverb/.<tt/degrees, minutes/ <tt/seconds/)
are fields of <tt/hms/.

<sect2>afromstr 
<p>
<tscreen><verb>
struct Angle afromstr(char *s)
</verb></tscreen>
<p>Fills all fields of the struct <tt/Angle/ given a string.
The units of the angle is supposed to be degrees.  The
string may contain the angle in decimal representation
or in hexadecimal representation. 
<p>Example of valid strings:<tt/"46.5069"/ or 
<tt/"46o30m25.64"/ or <tt/"46d30m25.64"/

<sect2> admsstr
<p>
<tscreen><verb>
char * admsstr (const struct Angle a, const int mode)
</verb></tscreen>
<p>Converts a <tt/struct Angle/ to a string, based on
its hexadecimal representation. The <tt/mode/ parameter
defimes the following formats :
<p>
<tscreen><verb>
mode = 0    returned string = "46 30 25.643346789"
mode = 1    returned string = "46d30m25.643346789"
mode = 2    returned string = "46\t30\t25.643346789"
</verb></tscreen>




